Here is the commit message:
[TransitionHandler] Set mouseTransparent of the whole view,
 fix bug

Here is the root cause:
The original code only toggled `mouseTransparent` on the `previousNode` (the outgoing view) during a transition, while leaving the `view` (the container) and the new incoming node fully interactive. This meant that while the transition animation was still playing, users could click on or interact with the new node before the transition truly completed, since only the old node was blocked from receiving mouse events. Additionally, the save/restore mechanism using `getProperties().put(MOUSE_TRANSPARENT, ...)` only preserved and restored the state of `previousNode`, but did nothing to prevent interaction with the currently transitioning-in node, allowing mouse events to leak through during the animation and causing unintended interactions (e.g., double-triggering actions, race conditions between animation state and user input). The fix addresses this by locking/unlocking mouse transparency on the entire `view` container instead of just the `previousNode`, ensuring that both the outgoing and incoming nodes are protected from mouse interaction for the whole duration of the transition.

Here is the patch:

     public void setContent(Node newView, AnimationProducer transition, Duration duration) {
         this.duration = duration;

         Timeline prev = animation;
         if (prev != null)
             prev.stop();

         updateContent(newView);

         transition.init(this);

         // runLater or "init" will not work
         Platform.runLater(() -> {
             Timeline nowAnimation = new Timeline();
             nowAnimation.getKeyFrames().addAll(transition.animate(this));
             nowAnimation.getKeyFrames().add(new KeyFrame(duration, e -> {
-                previousNode.setMouseTransparent((Boolean) previousNode.getProperties().get(MOUSE_TRANSPARENT));
+                view.setMouseTransparent(false);
                 view.getChildren().remove(previousNode);
             }));
             nowAnimation.play();
             animation = nowAnimation;
         });
     }

     private void updateContent(Node newView) {
         if (view.getWidth() > 0 && view.getHeight() > 0) {
             previousNode = currentNode;
             if (previousNode == null)
                 previousNode = NULL;
         } else
             previousNode = NULL;

         if (previousNode == newView)
             previousNode = NULL;

-        previousNode.getProperties().put(MOUSE_TRANSPARENT, previousNode.isMouseTransparent());
-        previousNode.setMouseTransparent(true);
+        view.setMouseTransparent(true);

         currentNode = newView;

         view.getChildren().setAll(previousNode, currentNode);
     }

-    private static final String MOUSE_TRANSPARENT = "TransitionHandler.MOUSE_TRANSPARENT";
     private static final StackPane NULL = new StackPane();
 }


